Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:50:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/47] VM display: frames reach the screen - NMXVGAFB grants
 system memory as VRAM, NMXAccel re-copies the front buffer at 60 Hz

- NMXVGAFB answers nvAllocVram/nvFreeVram with physically contiguous system memory (512 MB budget). IOAcceleratorFamily2
  wires WindowServer's display surfaces into video memory before a transaction may present them; without a grant
  every transaction failed (0xe00002be, "failed to wire down video map").
- NMXAccel (VM display only): the last presented surface is copied onto the panel at debug.nmxfb_front_hz (60)
  besides each transaction. The Metal plugin copies a frame out to the IOSurface after the GPU signals, while
  WindowServer presents on that signal, so a transaction could copy an empty frame and a static screen never sent
  another. Counter: debug.nmxfb_front_copies.

Result: WindowServer composites on the Xe VF and the login window and desktop show and update.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
